-- expect: T056
-- `Fn2` is one of the synthetic per-arity constructors that give a function
-- type's instance head a stable dispatch key. A function type is spelled
-- `fn a -> b`; the key is the compiler's own bookkeeping and no source ever
-- writes one. Accepting it produced a nominal type nothing inhabits, so the
-- mistake surfaced later as a mismatch whose expected side named a type no
-- program could produce. One arity higher, `Fn16`, already answered this way.
pub fn annotated_with_a_dispatch_key (x: Fn2 Int Text) -> Int = 1
